[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2530495465","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100229#issuecomment-2530495465","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100229","id":2530495465,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6W1Evp","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-10T05:51:40Z","updated_at":"2024-12-10T05:51:40Z","body":"Typed dictionaries are not compatible with typed ones, and `Object.set()` does not report errors as documented. Same with arrays.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2530495465/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2530624115","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100229#issuecomment-2530624115","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100229","id":2530624115,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6W1kJz","user":{"login":"mizuto","id":1930459,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzA0NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1930459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mizuto","html_url":"https://github.com/mizuto","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mizuto/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mizuto/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mizuto/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mizuto/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mizuto/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mizuto/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mizuto/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mizuto/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mizuto/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-10T07:14:53Z","updated_at":"2024-12-10T07:14:53Z","body":"Oops I missed the part where set() does not report error, though I think a warning would've been nice.\nI was able to get around this issue by simply doing.\n\n```\nget(dictionary_name).clear()\nfor key in result_dict.keys():\n    get(dictionary_name)[key] = result_dict[key]\n```\nThe target dictionary is typed while result_dict isn't.  \nIs this still intentional? It feels weirdly inconsistent to me.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2530624115/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2530696373","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100229#issuecomment-2530696373","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100229","id":2530696373,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6W11y1","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-10T07:45:26Z","updated_at":"2024-12-25T16:23:45Z","body":"> I was able to get around this issue by simply doing.\n> \n> ```\n> get(dictionary_name).clear()\n> for key in result_dict.keys():\n>     get(dictionary_name)[key] = result_dict[key]\n> ```\n\nYou can use [`Dictionary.assign()`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_dictionary.html#class-dictionary-method-assign) instead:\n\n```gdscript\nget(dictionary_name).assign(result_dict)\n```\n\n> Is this still intentional? It feels weirdly inconsistent to me.\n\nI agree that hiding the error is bad, but as far as I understand the `Object` API was designed this way for serialization, animation, inspector and other editor components. Changing this behavior can have many unexpected and unwanted effects.\n\nYou can use index/attribute syntax instead of `set()` and `get()` methods:\n\n```gdscript\nset(\"not_exist\", 123) # No error or warning.\nself[\"not_exist\"] = 123 # Runtime error.\nself.not_exist = 123 # Runtime error.\nnot_exist = 123 # Compile time error.\n```\n\nWe should document this somewhere because people have already asked why there is no compile time error about non-existent properties, see #98542.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2530696373/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2781603563","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100229#issuecomment-2781603563","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100229","id":2781603563,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ly-br","user":{"login":"cromachina","id":82557197,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgyNTU3MTk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/82557197?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cromachina","html_url":"https://github.com/cromachina","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cromachina/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cromachina/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cromachina/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cromachina/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cromachina/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cromachina/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cromachina/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cromachina/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cromachina/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-06T19:38:56Z","updated_at":"2025-04-06T19:38:56Z","body":"`Object.set` not producing an error for typed dictionaries and arrays got me some confusing bugs when doing some typed object deserialization.\n\nSome example problem code of extracting an object's field from a file:\n```gdscript\n\tvar obj : Object = registry[cls_name].new()\n\tvar prop_count := file.get_32()\n\tfor i in range(prop_count):\n\t\tvar prop_name := file.get_pascal_string()\n\t\tvar prop_value : Variant = read_variant(file)\n\t\tobj.set(prop_name, prop_value) # Silently drops the assignment if the property is a typed array or dictionary\n```\n\nThe version of the code that is fixed with a type check on the target property, followed by a call to `assign`:\n```gdscript\n\tvar obj : Object = registry[cls_name].new()\n\tvar prop_count := file.get_32()\n\tfor _i in range(prop_count):\n\t\tvar prop_name := file.get_pascal_string()\n\t\tvar prop_read_value : Variant = read_variant(file)\n\t\tvar prop_obj = obj.get(prop_name)\n\t\tvar type = typeof(prop_obj)\n\t\tif type in [TYPE_ARRAY, TYPE_DICTIONARY] and prop_obj.is_typed():\n\t\t\tprop_obj.assign(prop_read_value)\n\t\telse:\n\t\t\tobj.set(prop_name, prop_read_value)\n```","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2781603563/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]